//
// Normative rule menvcfg_sse_rdonly0 (src/priv/machine.adoc):
//   When menvcfg.SSE is 0, the henvcfg.SSE and senvcfg.SSE fields are read-only zero.
//
// Context:
//   SSE is bit 3 of menvcfg, senvcfg and henvcfg. When menvcfg.SSE is set again, the fields' values
//     are UNSPECIFIED until written (field modulation), so they are written before being read.
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/1509: xenvcfg masking (read-only zero) follows
//     the CSR field-modulation rule.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. menvcfg.SSE=1: senvcfg.SSE (and henvcfg.SSE with H) can be set and cleared.
//   2. Set both, then clear menvcfg.SSE: both read 0.
//   3. While menvcfg.SSE=0, csrs and csrw of SSE=1 leave them reading 0, and the writes do not
//     change the other bits of senvcfg/henvcfg.
//   4. menvcfg.SSE=1 again: after a write of 1, they read 1.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 748
//

